From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: blackhat-7 <44942105+blackhat-7@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 01:27:06 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 23/33] NVIDIA helper for the HIP engine: a CUDA plugin serves
 --expert-cache-device1

STRATA_NV_HELPER=libstrata_nvhelper.so (target strata_nvhelper in a CUDA build of this tree) makes the helper tier an
NVIDIA card while the primary stays HIP: the plugin is dlopen'ed (RTLD_LOCAL, only snv_api exported), owns the card's
expert slots, and runs the grouped expert kernels on it; everything crosses through pinned host memory, as the
same-make helpers do.  Measured on an RX 7900 XTX + RTX 4070 (Swift IQ3_XXS, generate mode, priced windows):
static ranking code +11%, prose +20%, edit +40%; with the adaptive tiers on code +4%, prose +3%, edit +26%.

- per layer: the engine quantizes the rows to q8_1 on the CPU (bit for bit the GPU quantizer: tmp parity test), one
  kernel stages metadata and rows onto the card, the grouped kernels run, one kernel writes the rows back in 16-byte
  stores (the down kernel's 4-byte writes over the chipset's x4 link cost 3x the compute)
- adaptive tier on the card (adapt_nv): hot CPU misses replace its coldest experts and its copies of experts the
  primary now holds; fills on their own copy stream from the arena, pinned for CUDA too
- the launch runs inside the CPU pool's first phase (pool pre-drain hook); STRATA_NV_PRE_DRAIN=0 for the old order
- STRATA_NV_TIMING=1: the card's own time per step; STRATA_NV_ADAPT_SWAPS: its swaps a round
- sm_89 joins sm_120 in the fused gate/up + SwiGLU default (CUDA builds only)
